---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND, CONTACT, sites } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About Tidy Magpie"
  description="Tidy Magpie is a small independent publisher in Australia making single-subject reference sites. Who runs it, why the name, and how the sites are made."
  path="/about/"
>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>About {BRAND}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {BRAND} is a small independent publisher based in Australia. It makes reference sites that each cover one
      subject properly, and it started in November 2026.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we make</h2>
      <p>
        Some questions get looked up over and over: which gift a character likes, whether the aurora is worth a drive
        tonight, which achievements are left. The answers tend to be scattered across announcements, store pages and
        data feeds. Each {BRAND} site gathers one subject's answers into pages you can scan, filter or tick off.
      </p>
      <p>There are {sites.length} sites so far:</p>
      <ul>
        {sites.map((s) => (
          <li><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Why the name</h2>
      <p>
        Magpies have a reputation, not entirely deserved, for carrying off anything that catches their eye. We do
        collect. The tidy part is putting each fact where you can find it, with a note of where it came from.
      </p>

      <h2>How the sites are made</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          They are researched, written and coded with AI tools, under human direction. A person decides what gets made
          and what gets published.
        </li>
        <li>They are plain static pages. There are no accounts, and progress you save stays in your browser.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The rules for sourcing and checking are set out in <a href="/how-we-work/">How we work</a>.</p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        {BRAND} is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by the companies and agencies whose games and data its
        sites cover. Game names and other trademarks belong to their owners.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections and questions are welcome at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. The
        <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> says what helps.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
